WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.385 --> 00:00:02.184
- Now, explain all 
of this with regard

00:00:02.184 --> 00:00:03.629
to the New York Jets.

00:00:03.629 --> 00:00:05.154
(laughter)

00:00:05.154 --> 00:00:06.984
- I desperately wanna 
buy them, Larry.

00:00:06.984 --> 00:00:07.856
- You do?

00:00:07.856 --> 00:00:08.695
- Yes, I do.

00:00:08.695 --> 00:00:12.975
- Why this, you're so level
headed and on top of things.

00:00:12.975 --> 00:00:13.776
- [Gary] Yes.

00:00:13.776 --> 00:00:16.184
- But sports things 
are a fan thing.

00:00:16.184 --> 00:00:18.386
You know look, 
I'll tell you the truth.

00:00:18.386 --> 00:00:19.994
When I came to America,

00:00:19.994 --> 00:00:21.855
in Queens and in Dover,

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:23.145
I couldn't speak English.

00:00:23.145 --> 00:00:25.075
Barely speaking any English 
and they were playing football

00:00:25.075 --> 00:00:26.468
and my friend 
Eric Godfrey's like,

00:00:26.468 --> 00:00:27.772
"What team do you like?"

00:00:27.772 --> 00:00:29.694
And I was like literally that 
kid that didn't speak English.

00:00:29.694 --> 00:00:32.406
I was like, 
probably did one of those.

00:00:32.406 --> 00:00:33.584
And he says, "You're a Jets fan."

00:00:33.584 --> 00:00:35.326
And so I went home,
I was like, "I'm a Jets fan."

00:00:35.326 --> 00:00:38.715
It was my first American thing.

00:00:38.715 --> 00:00:41.526
So they all had Jets jerseys,
we would play and I wanted

00:00:41.526 --> 00:00:43.666
a Jets jersey 'cause I fell 
in love with the Jets

00:00:43.666 --> 00:00:45.216
but we were poor.

00:00:45.216 --> 00:00:46.646
We couldn't afford 
stuff like that.

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:47.705
It's not what immigrants do.

00:00:47.705 --> 00:00:49.518
You don't go out and
buy a $30 Jets jersey.

00:00:49.518 --> 00:00:51.566
So, my mom knitted me one.

00:00:51.566 --> 00:00:52.457
She made it.

00:00:52.457 --> 00:00:53.867
On the back of this it 
has my favorite number,

00:00:53.867 --> 00:00:55.466
number 5 and says Gary.

00:00:55.466 --> 00:00:57.337
And I literally 
wore it everyday.

00:00:57.337 --> 00:00:58.619
It's my prized possession.

00:00:58.619 --> 00:01:00.427
It's literally my 
prized possession.

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:02.367
It just symbolizes 
where we came from

00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:05.406
which was very, very, very
humble beginnings.

00:01:05.406 --> 00:01:07.176
And I've created 
a fairy tale in my mind,

00:01:07.176 --> 00:01:08.934
somewhere around 
2nd or 3rd grade,

00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:10.456
that I was gonna go from

00:01:10.456 --> 00:01:12.427
not being able 
to afford a jersey,

00:01:12.427 --> 00:01:13.898
to owning the 
whole damn thing.

00:01:13.898 --> 00:01:16.218
Quest to buy the Jets

00:01:16.218 --> 00:01:18.098
is my happiness.

00:01:18.098 --> 00:01:19.098
Always wondered why

00:01:19.098 --> 00:01:20.248
I always said 
I would buy the Jets

00:01:20.248 --> 00:01:24.628
and I wonder how much 
all that has to do with it.

00:01:24.628 --> 00:01:26.928
It's a big deal to me.

00:01:26.928 --> 00:01:28.069
It's a big deal.

